;&lt;p&gt;Own utility and regulatory stakeholder management across multiple European jurisdictions, building strategic relationships with TSOs, DSOs, national regulators, and ACER to accelerate connection timelines and unlock constrained capacity&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Drive energy markets and policy strategy for AI compute facilities, monitoring EU network codes, national grid codes and regulatory developments and engaging policymakers to address grid capacity challenges and expedite approval processes for critical infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Partner with engineering and delivery teams to translate energy market dynamics and network constraints into actionable capacity acceleration strategies that align procurement schedules with aggressive project timelines&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Develop deep market intelligence on regional power availability across target European markets, transmission constraints, and connection queue dynamics to inform site selection and deployment strategy&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Structure innovative commercial frameworks and partnership models — including PPAs, network use of system arrangements, and behind-the-meter solutions — that enable faster power delivery and mitigate grid capacity risks across Anthropic&#39;s European datacentre portfolio&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have 15+ years of experience in energy procurement, utility development, or power markets for large-scale infrastructure projects, with substantial exposure to European energy markets across multiple jurisdictions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have deep expertise in EU electricity markets (day-ahead, intraday and balancing markets), national capacity mechanisms, network connection processes, and transmission system planning (including ENTSO-E Ten-Year Network Development Plans and national network development plans)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have experience securing 100+ MW of power capacity and navigating complex network connection agreements, Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs), or other offtake agreement structures in Europe&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Are proficient in analysing energy market dynamics, regulatory frameworks (EU network codes, national grid codes and jurisdictional instruments), and grid constraints to inform strategic decision-making&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have strong stakeholder management skills and experience building relationships with TSOs, DSOs, national regulators (such as BNetzA, CRU, ACM, CRE, and others), ACER, policymakers and critical equipment vendors&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have excellent communication skills and can translate complex grid and regulatory dynamics into actionable business strategies for technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have some of the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Past experience with energy procurement specifically for datacentres, high-performance computing, or AI/ML infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with hyperscale infrastructure requirements and the unique power demands of large-scale AI training and inference workloads&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience with regulatory affairs, energy policy advocacy, or engagement with national regulators, TSOs, ACER, ENTSO-E, and the European Commission (DG ENER) and national energy ministries&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Background in transmission planning, grid connection studies (including grid code compliance and connection agreement processes), or grid capacity analysis under EU network codes and national grid codes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Understanding of emerging grid technologies (battery energy storage systems, demand response, virtual power plants, distributed energy resources) and how they can accelerate capacity delivery across European markets&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Track record of structuring creative solutions to overcome grid constraints and compressed timelines in competitive power markets, including EU renewables acceleration areas / go-to areas and congested bidding zones and network regions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
