ecutive relationships with hardware suppliers and power and infrastructure OEMs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Own supply risk, including single-source exposure, geography, tariffs and export controls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Identify supply gaps before they impact the business.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have 15+ years in strategic sourcing or supply chain for semiconductors, hardware, or datacenter infrastructure, and have led a function rather than a single category.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have built a sourcing organization through rapid growth, including managers who lead teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have negotiated capacity or long-term supply agreements at multibillion-dollar scale with executive counterparts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have deep experience in either semiconductor supply (foundry, memory or hardware) or data center and power infrastructure equipment, and the judgment to lead the other.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Can make hard allocation calls and explain the trade-offs to executives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have strong written communication and executive presence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Built a sourcing function from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sourced for other kinds of hardware, such as robotics or manufacturing equipment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sourced across the US, Europe and Asia, including for an international data center portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
