&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Head of National Security Sales (DoW/IC) at Anthropic, you&#39;ll lead and scale our national security sales organization to drive the adoption of safe, frontier AI across the Department of War and the Intelligence Community. You&#39;ll leverage your deep understanding of defense and intelligence missions and proven sales leadership expertise to build a high-performing team while establishing strategic relationships with key defense and intelligence organizations. Working closely with GTM, product, policy, engineering and marketing teams, you&#39;ll define and execute our go-to-market strategy for the DoW and IC while maintaining the highest standards of security and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and scale a national security sales team covering the DoW and IC, including hiring top talent, setting clear performance expectations, and providing ongoing coaching and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive go-to-market strategies for the DoW (including the military services, combatant commands, OSW, and defense agencies) and the IC, including market segmentation, competitive positioning, and revenue forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anchor the team&#39;s work in mission impact: prioritize opportunities where safe, frontier AI materially changes how commands and agencies plan, analyze, and operate, and measure success by outcomes delivered to those who serve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own overall national security revenue targets and ensure team performance against quotas, while providing visibility into pipeline health and deal progression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win new business across the DoW and IC by helping commands, components, and agencies integrate AI into their technology stacks and mission workflows to accelerate delivery and mission outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and refine sales processes, methodologies, and playbooks specific to DoW and IC procurement, including FAR/DFARS compliance, classified and unclassified contracting pathways, and agency-specific security and accreditation requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage strategic relationships with cloud service providers, systems integrators, and Defense Industrial Base partners to create scalable go-to-market motions across classified and unclassified environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize market feedback and customer insights to inform product roadmap and competitive strategy, working closely with product and marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with legal, compliance, security, and delivery teams to ensure successful contract execution and customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visibility and relationships with senior military, civilian, and IC leadership while empowering your team to own day-to-day customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement metrics, reporting, and performance management systems to drive team accountability and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Anthropic at industry events and with key stakeholders, establishing our brand as the trusted AI partner for the national security community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of enterprise sales experience with 5+ years managing sales teams selling into the DoW and/or IC, with a proven track record of scaling revenue and building high-performing organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build, maintain, and leverage senior military, civilian, and leadership relationships across the DoW and IC—with an existing network of contacts across the national security community strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of DoW and IC missions, organizational structures, modernization initiatives, and technology adoption patterns across multiple services, commands, and agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active security clearance (TS/SCI required) with ability to discuss capabilities in classified environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to hire, develop, and retain top sales talent while creating a culture of performance and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing go-to-market strategies for emerging technologies in the national security space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with defense and intelligence contracting vehicles, procurement mechanisms (including OTAs and IDIQs), and compliance and accreditation requirements such as FAR/DFARS, FedRAMP, and DoW Impact Levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of consistently exceeding team revenue targets and building predictable, scalable sales motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and manage strategic channel partnerships and ecosystem relationships, including cloud providers, systems integrators, and Defense Industrial Base primes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and relationship-building skills across all levels, from technical teams to senior military, civilian, and IC leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing sales methodologies, CRM systems, and performance management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for safe and ethical AI development, with the ability to articulate its importance in national security contexts and build trust with DoW and IC stakeholders&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
