&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Strategic Startups at Anthropic, you will own the strategy, organization, and commercial outcomes for Anthropic&#39;s relationships with the world&#39;s most important AI-native startups. This is the segment where the next generation of category-defining companies is being built on Claude, and where Anthropic&#39;s commercial, product, and partnership decisions compound fastest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of Account Executives who own Anthropic&#39;s most strategic AI-native accounts, and be accountable for a revenue line spanning expansion, retention, and net-new strategic wins. Beyond running the business, you will define what &quot;strategic&quot; means for Anthropic in the startup ecosystem: which companies we bet on, how we structure partnerships with them, how we engage investors and accelerators, and how the signal from this segment shapes our product roadmap and go-to-market model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a member of the GTM leadership team and a visible voice for Anthropic in the startup and venture community, helping ensure that the companies defining the future of AI choose to build it safely, and with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set the multi-year strategy for Anthropic&#39;s Strategic Startups business, including segmentation, coverage model, partnership structures, and investment priorities, and secure executive alignment on it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build, lead, and scale a high-performing team of Account Executives, including hiring, coaching, and developing sellers and establishing a strong operating cadence across the team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the segment&#39;s revenue plan and P&amp;amp;L-level outcomes, including forecasting, capacity planning, quota design, and resource allocation, with direct accountability to GTM and company leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personally lead Anthropic&#39;s relationships with a portfolio of the highest-leverage AI-native startups, engaging founders, CEOs, and CTOs on multi-year commercial, technical, and partnership agreements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and negotiate novel commercial and partnership structures (credits programs, strategic pricing, co-development, joint go-to-market) that create durable, mutually beneficial relationships with breakout companies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the executive voice of the startup segment inside Anthropic, bringing structured customer and market insight to Product, Engineering, Pricing, and Finance and influencing roadmap and packaging decisions accordingly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Enterprise Sales, Solutions, Partnerships, and Customer Success leadership to define handoffs, shared accounts, and escalation paths as startups scale into enterprise customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish the systems of record for the segment: account planning, customer health, executive business reviews, deal governance, and the metrics leadership uses to run the business&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent Anthropic externally with founders, investors, and at industry events, articulating our approach to safe, frontier AI and why it matters for companies building on it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lean in to support building Anthropic&#39;s presence across the startup ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 15+ years of experience in enterprise or technical software sales, with 7+ years leading sales teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have been a founder or have worked previously as a Business Development leader securing large contracts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have owned a significant revenue line with full accountability for plan, forecast, and results, and have a track record of consistently outperforming it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built or materially scaled a sales or account management organization, including designing coverage models, compensation plans, and operating rhythms&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring deep, first-hand familiarity with the startup ecosystem, including relationships with founders, venture investors, and accelerators, and an instinct for identifying which early-stage companies will become the ones that matter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have sold or led sales of technical, consumption-based, or platform products (APIs, infrastructure, developer tools, ML/AI), and are credible in conversations with technical founders and CTOs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have structured and closed complex, non-standard commercial and partnership agreements at the executive level&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are a strong cross-functional leader who has influenced product, pricing, and go-to-market decisions well beyond your own organization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are analytically rigorous and comfortable making decisions with imperfect data in a rapidly evolving market&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are motivated by Anthropic&#39;s mission and care about how frontier AI is deployed, not just how fast it grows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have led a startups or emerging-companies segment at a cloud, infrastructure, or AI platform company through a period of hypergrowth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have founder, operator, or venture experience, and understand the pressures and decision-making of a high-growth startup from the inside&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built ecosystem programs (startup credits, accelerator partnerships, investor programs) that meaningfully drove adoption of a developer platform&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have hired and developed leaders who went on to run their own organizations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have experience leading through a market where the product and competitive landscape shifts quarterly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$550,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$750,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world&#39;s engineers want to get the most out of Claude. At Anthropic, technical instruction already happens everywhere: our Applied AI and Forward Deployed Engineering teams teach customers and partners, and engineers across the company help others learn to build with Claude. Today that instruction is a shared responsibility, delivered alongside people&#39;s primary roles. As demand grows, we need to turn that distributed expertise into a dedicated technical instruction function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build that function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the first person at Anthropic whose full-time job is technical instruction. You&#39;ll spend your first year primarily in the classroom teaching engineers, architects, and other technical practitioners. You&#39;ll also build the people, standards, and systems that let Anthropic&#39;s technical instruction scale far beyond the people we directly employ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player-coach role. From day one you manage a small bench of instructors. You set the bar for what &quot;ready to teach&quot; means, decide who is cleared to teach a given module in Anthropic&#39;s technical programs, and assess facilitators from our training partners against that bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re an engineer who teaches and a teacher who has led other teachers. You can build an agent live in front of a skeptical engineer, diagnose what isn&#39;t working in a technical lab, and make the material better. You can also watch an experienced instructor teach, tell them their session isn&#39;t ready yet, and coach them to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Head of Technical Enablement. The role is based in San Francisco with some travel expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead from the front.&lt;/strong&gt; Teach hands-on sessions to new Applied AI engineers, our field teams, and partner cohorts, in rooms from 12-person labs to 100-person training days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the instructor bench.&lt;/strong&gt; Hire and develop instructors and curriculum developers. Decide contract renewals, and recommend conversions to full-time, against criteria you define.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the quality bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the observation rubric, dry-run protocol, and cleared-to-teach process for every instructor-led technical session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale through train-the-trainer.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the bar the Lead Technical Instructor&#39;s train-the-trainer program teaches to, for internal experts, contract instructors, and partner facilitators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn expertise into instruction.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn internal experts&#39; content into sessions and labs that work in a live room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable programs without owning them.&lt;/strong&gt; Staff other teams&#39; programs with cleared instructors, and own the quality of instruction inside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure and improve.&lt;/strong&gt; Report learner pass rates per instructor each month, and act on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of relevant professional experience&lt;/strong&gt; across software engineering, solutions engineering, developer advocacy, technical education, or related technical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years of hands-on technical instruction.&lt;/strong&gt; You have taught engineers live and hands-on, across audience sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production engineering.&lt;/strong&gt; You have written and shipped production software and engage credibly with experienced engineers on architecture and debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recent hands-on AI development.&lt;/strong&gt; In your last three years of work, you have built or debugged applications with LLM APIs, agent frameworks, tool use, MCP, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; You have managed instructors, trainers, developer advocates, or solutions engineers, including hiring and performance management, and kept teaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instructor development.&lt;/strong&gt; You have designed or run a train-the-trainer program, instructor certification, or observation framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;San Francisco location.&lt;/strong&gt; You are based in San Francisco or willing to relocate with our relocation support, can be in the office every day a program runs, 3 days in a normal week, and can travel 25 to 30 percent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio of sessions you taught and a rubric or certification you designed, shared only if you have the right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building an instruction or developer-education function from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a contractor instructor bench, or clearing instructors across regions from recordings or trained observers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily use of Claude Code or a comparable agentic coding tool, or building on Claude through Amazon Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, or Microsoft Foundry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep enthusiasm for AI and real care about building it responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
