&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Endpoint team (Client Platform Engineering) manages the laptops and handsets every Anthropic employee works on, plus the infrastructure underneath them. We treat the fleet as a distributed platform, not a collection of devices, and every piece of configuration ships as code through pull requests, CI, staging, and a canary group. Today the mobile side of the fleet is BYOD. This role exists to change that. You will design and implement a corporate-issued mobile device program (managed company phones and managed Apple accounts) in every region Anthropic operates in, and take it from early design to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is deliberately lean and runs with high autonomy. You’ll define what a corporate mobile program looks like at Anthropic and own the platform decisions that get it there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the corporate-issued mobile device program: device standards, what we issue to whom, and how the program grows from a first region to everywhere Anthropic operates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global logistics of issuing hardware: procurement partners, regional coverage, spares, and refresh cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring mobile configuration into the team’s config-as-code pipeline so mobile policies are reviewed, tested, and progressively rolled out like the rest of the fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build zero-touch enrollment: Apple Business Manager and ADE with managed Apple accounts on iOS, the zero-touch equivalent on Android, so a new phone works the first time without hands-on setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own policy, compliance, and device lifecycle for the corporate fleet, from issue to wipe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build telemetry on the corporate fleet: which devices are checking in, OS and patch state, drift between reported and actual state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own managed app distribution for mobile, from app approval through update rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Corporate Security on device posture, device trust signals, and travel devices for international trips&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide how corporate-issued and BYOD coexist, and own that boundary as the program rolls out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have owned a global or multi-region mobile device program end to end, with 8+ years managing corporate fleets at thousands-of-devices scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go deep on iOS device management: enrollment flows, Apple Business Manager and ADE, APNs and certificate lifecycle, declarative device management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with Android device management and can hold your own in a mixed fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat device configuration as code and have moved past clicking in consoles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have run the infrastructure under an MDM, not just administered a SaaS console: a self-hosted MDM server, AWS, Terraform, and configuration that ships as code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built or launched a corporate device program, not just operated one, and can decide how it coexists with BYOD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excel at ambiguous problems that touch several teams at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical concepts clearly to any audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;View IT Engineering as requiring product engineering rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear documentation as a natural part of your workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed ChromeOS devices alongside a mobile fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have run a device program across multiple regions and dealt with the logistics that come with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built automated, progressive rollout systems with promotion gated on telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring proficiency in Swift for building device tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have used LLMs to automate operational work, or are excited to make Claude a teammate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python and shell scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;iOS and Android platform internals (depth on iOS, working knowledge of Android)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern MDM or UEM platforms (Jamf, Intune, Workspace ONE, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running the infrastructure under an MDM (self-hosted servers, AWS GCP, Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Querying live device state at fleet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile device lifecycle automation (enrollment, policy, patching, app distribution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitOps and CI for configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Endpoint security fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deadline to apply: None. Applications will be received on a rolling basis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
