&lt;li&gt;Build the brand tooling layer: internal tools, integrations, and Claude-in-the-loop workflows that let designers, writers, and marketers publish safely without engineering as a bottleneck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with design and editorial on creative technology, data visualizations, interactive explainers, campaign experiences, that need real engineering, not a template&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align web engineering work with Marketing, Product, Comms, and core Engineering, and say no to what doesn&#39;t move brand and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in software engineering, 5+ managing engineers, with that time spent as an engineering manager inside a marketing, brand, or design engineering organization specifically, not just a product engineering one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owned a high-traffic marketing or brand web surface end to end: CMS, frontend, infrastructure, and the publishing workflow around it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong frontend depth yourself, TypeScript, React, modern CSS, a modern headless CMS, and a real preference for staying close to the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built tooling that made non-engineers faster and safer, with a concrete story of what changed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped under real launch pressure with cross-functional partners, without dropping the quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating at the seam between Design, Marketing, and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep interest in AI and excitement about putting Claude into the build and publish loop itself, not just on the page&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Held a Head of Web Engineering or equivalent platform lead title at a product company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built localization and multi region web infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
