&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Beneficial Deployments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beneficial Deployments ensures AI reaches and benefits the communities that need it most. We partner with nonprofits, governments, and mission-driven organizations to deploy Claude in education, global health, economic mobility, and life sciences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partnerships Manager to help extend Anthropic&#39;s health work into US public health. Building on our existing global health portfolio, you&#39;ll help shape how we engage the US public health system and manage a set of partnerships across federal, state, and local levels. Because this is an emerging area for the team, the role blends partnership management with meaningful contribution to strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person combines credibility in the US public health ecosystem, enough technical fluency to be a real thought partner on AI deployment, and comfort operating in a space that&#39;s still taking shape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is distinct from our Account Executive function: while AEs drive scaled adoption of Anthropic&#39;s core products, Partnership Managers build deep partnerships that require custom deployments, research collaboration, and hands-on program design. You&#39;ll work with a smaller portfolio of flagship partners where the goal is driving impact metrics and creating learnings that benefit the broader ecosystem.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to Anthropic&#39;s US public health strategy, working closely with the team lead to identify priority partners and use cases and bringing field insights back to inform our broader health work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own a portfolio of flagship deployments, coordinating with Applied AI, product, policy, and GTM teams to deliver impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Source, evaluate, and onboard new partners; structure engagements that work within government procurement, data governance, and privacy constraints&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate partner needs into deployment plans that account for legacy systems and workforce realities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support the creation of shared resources and digital public goods that help the broader field use AI responsibly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the evidence base by partnering with academic and evaluation organizations to study what works&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent Anthropic at public health convenings and with funders and policymakers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help shape team processes as we grow this area; hand off opportunities better suited to scaled sales or public sector motions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel to partner sites and to SF headquarters every ~6 weeks for those based outside SF (~20% travel)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Might Be a Good Fit If You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of experience in US public health, health policy, or public sector health innovation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years managing external partnerships, multi-stakeholder initiatives, or programs that span government and civil society&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep relationships and credibility in the US public health ecosystem — you know the key players at CDC, state health departments, major schools of public health, and the foundations that fund this work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A working understanding of how federal, state, and local public health agencies operate, fund programs, and adopt new technology&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical fluency to engage credibly on AI concepts, understand LLM capabilities and limitations, and partner effectively with technical teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building programs or portfolios in early-stage environments where the playbook is still being written&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High agency and comfort with ambiguity; you thrive when the playbook doesn&#39;t exist yet&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A genuine drive to strengthen the public health system and the communities it serves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An MPH or related credential&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Candidates May Also Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience inside a federal or state health agency (CDC, HHS, a state DOH) or at an organization that works closely with them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in epidemiology, ideally with hands-on surveillance experience at a state, local, or federal health agency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working in a global context&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience at a healthtech company, AI organization, or in a product-adjacent role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
