&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is seeking a Privacy Counsel to join our Legal team. You&#39;ll counsel on complex privacy issues and build the processes and programs that address privacy and data protection in a global context. This is a unique opportunity to join a dynamic and growing team, where you will have the chance to shape the company&#39;s privacy and data protection strategy and compliance program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of novel legal questions, fast-moving product development, and a high-profile regulatory environment, partnering cross-functionally with Legal, Integrity &amp;amp; Compliance, Safeguards, Security, Policy, Research and Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counsel product, research and engineering teams across the model and product lifecycles, applying laws written before frontier AI with clarity and fresh thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical architecture into clear, actionable risk advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver integrated guidance on safety, security and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead privacy on Anthropic&#39;s most strategic deals and partnerships, opening creative paths for novel technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate privacy and data protection terms in enterprise, platform and partnership commercial agreements, including DPAs, BAAs, data sharing agreements and cross-border transfer terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead privacy diligence on mergers and acquisitions, and support corporate governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with counsel and privacy colleagues on joint analysis, bringing competing views together into a single, well-reasoned position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD from an accredited law school and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience advising a technology business (in-house or at a leading law firm) on privacy and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience drafting and negotiating data protection agreements, such as DPAs, BAAs and data sharing agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of key global privacy laws, including those of the Americas, EEA and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and engage with technical documentation, such as system designs and architecture diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent legal writing, including clear, concise advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
