&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Claude is now good at security work. It finds and fixes vulnerabilities in real codebases, triages alerts, and reasons about how an attacker would move through a system, and it improves with every model we ship. Many security platforms build on Claude and we shipped our first security product this year (Claude Security).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead the cybersecurity product at Anthropic. That means setting the strategy, deciding what we build and where we partner, shipping products, and being the company&#39;s voice with CISOs, security vendors, and researchers. Some of this is 0→1 (our first-party products are a few months old and the next ones don&#39;t exist yet) and some of it is scaling what already works. Security touches nearly every team at the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set Anthropic&#39;s cybersecurity product portfolio strategy and be accountable for the results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship security products. Vulnerability discovery and remediation in Claude Code today and a broader set of capabilities in the future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Anthropic on security externally, with CISOs, vendors, researchers, governments, and press.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with research. Know where the model falls short on security tasks and help build a plan to improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with safeguards and policy on model access for Cybersecurity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the cross-functional threads moving across research, engineering, sales, safeguards, policy, legal, and comms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve spent meaningful time in security, whether building security products, running a security team, or doing the work yourself in application security, detection and response, vulnerability research, or offensive security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built products or businesses from scratch and taken them to paying customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You design for where the models will be rather than where they are. You treat what the model can&#39;t do yet as a research target with a reliability bar, and you know what to ship in the meantime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong product judgment and enough technical depth to read a finding and tell whether it&#39;s real.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re willing to do the unglamorous work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate well with CISOs, researchers, and executives alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience building and shipping products, especially in the security space .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI products: evaluations, model behavior as part of the product surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background or experience working closely with infrastructure/platform teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment with ability to go deep on security and infrastructure topics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured thinking and ability to break down complex compliance requirements into shippable features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
