&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Training and serving frontier AI models requires data center capacity at a scale and pace that conventional delivery models were not built for. Anthropic&#39;s Data Center Capacity Delivery team embeds with developers, general contractors, and third-party partners to take leased and partnered sites from deal close through floor access and operational handover as fast as they can safely be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Regional Manager, you&#39;ll own delivery across a regional portfolio of active and upcoming projects. You&#39;ll build and lead the team of Senior Delivery Managers and third-party partners who sit on those sites, set the standards they execute to, and step in yourself where a project needs it. You are the executive-level interface to our developer partners in the region and the intake point for projects handed over from our transaction team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional role: you&#39;ll work daily with our transaction, design engineering, facility operations and commissioning, deployment, and safety teams, and with developers, GCs, and owner&#39;s-representative firms on the ground.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MOC (Mission + Outcomes + Competencies)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deliver the region’s data center projects to floor access as fast as they can safely be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every active project in the region delivered against early-floor-access and floor-access milestones.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Senior Delivery Manager team hired and led; owner’s-rep partners contracted and managed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Delivery standards (schedule, quality, change control, reporting) enforced across the portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Executive reporting on progress vs plan and regional capacity projections in place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Senior owner- or GC-side mission-critical delivery leadership.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Builds and leads multi-project teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Executive-level developer and GC relationship management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Leads on site through presence; owns outcomes where no process exists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lead. This is a role where leadership trumps management and process. You are expected to be on the region&#39;s sites enough to shape the culture, approach, and aggressiveness that define the extended teams there — across the portfolio, not one project — and to impact outcomes in a favorable manner.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Be a force multiplier. Hire, develop, empower, and lead the Senior Delivery Managers on those sites, and raise the skillset developers, contractors, owner&#39;s-rep partners, and key trades bring to every project in the region; plan resourcing and headcount as the portfolio grows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Own portfolio execution for the region — schedule, quality, and safety outcomes on every active project, measured against early-floor-access and floor-access milestones. You are empowered and have autonomy to own this region&#39;s record of performance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Drive ownership and influence both inside and outside contractual structures: select, scope, contract, and manage owner&#39;s-rep and project-management partners; where contracts, incentives, or culture get in the way of speed, change them, and replace partners when performance or culture slips&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Set and enforce delivery standards across projects — integrated schedule, quality requirements, change control, reporting, and tools — and validate that they are met&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Identify blockers early and clear them across developer, GC, and trade layers; step in on site where a project needs it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have 10+ years delivering data center or other mission-critical construction, including several as the owner&#39;s or GC&#39;s senior leader on a project campus&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have led a multi-project portfolio and built the team that delivered it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Know the end-to-end development process — entitlements and permitting, design, long-lead equipment, construction, commissioning, and handover — well enough to direct partners rather than take their word for it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have managed developer, GC, and third-party relationships at the executive level and can move them from arm&#39;s-length contract administration to shared urgency&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lead through presence: you expect to be on site most of the time and to set the pace and culture of extended teams you don&#39;t directly employ&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Communicate clearly with technical and non-specialist stakeholders and hold a position when challenged&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Are comfortable with ambiguity and with owning outcomes where no process exists yet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hyperscale data center delivery experience on the owner, developer, or GC side&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience with the Australian and Japanese/Korean market — its contractors, permitting regimes, and contractual norms&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with lease, construction, and development contract structures and how to align their incentives around speed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
