&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Manager, Workforce Accounting to join Anthropic&#39;s Corporate Accounting Operations team. You will own every number tied to how we pay, equip and reward the people who work here: payroll and accrued compensation, stock-based compensation benefits and relocation, commissions, contingent workers, and travel and expense. Reporting to the Head of Corporate Accounting, you will lead a team of accountants while staying hands-on; reviewing close materials, owning your own accounts, and serving as the first escalation point for the judgment calls in your domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workforce is one of the fastest-moving areas of our P&amp;amp;L. As headcount grows across new entities and geographies, equity programmes are becoming more complex, and the systems that feed payroll, equity and expense data into the ledger are still being wired together. This is a build role: you will write the policies and SOPs your team operates against, design the controls, shape the system integrations, and use Claude and other tools to automate the work that does not need to be manual. We are looking for someone who has built accounting infrastructure in high-growth environments before and wants to do it again at one of the most important companies in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the workforce portfolio through month-end and quarter-end close — payroll and accrued compensation, bonus, vacation, severance and retention accruals, benefits, relocation, commissions, contingent workers, and T&amp;amp;E — including reconciliations, journal entries and variance commentary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own stock-based compensation accounting end to end: expense recognition under ASC 718, cash-settlement matching, equity roll-forwards, and reconciliation of preferred stock, common stock and additional paid-in capital to the equity administration platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the headcount and compensation reporting that underpins close analytics and cost allocations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure every close deliverable is audit-ready, with clear documentation of positions and supporting evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical accounting and policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, own and maintain accounting policies and SOPs across the workforce domain — payroll accruals, ASC 718, commissions (ASC 340-40), contingent worker classification, and T&amp;amp;E — and evolve them as compensation programmes change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review technical memos prepared by your team; ensure conclusions are well-supported and consistent with US GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technical Accounting on new or modified equity awards, plan changes and other non-routine compensation arrangements, and translate guidance into procedures the team can execute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the workforce-related footnotes and disclosures — employee benefit plans, stockholders&#39; equity and net loss per share — and the external audit responses that support them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operate SOX controls across payroll, equity and T&amp;amp;E; review control evidence and own timely remediation of any gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish cut-off and completeness controls around payroll registers, equity administration data and expense platforms so that what hits the ledger ties to source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems and automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the integrations between our ERP and the payroll, equity administration, commissions and T&amp;amp;E platforms — translating accounting requirements into specifications and test criteria, and owning data integrity once live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify repetitive, rules-based work across the team&#39;s workflows and build scalable solutions, including with Claude, to automate or replace it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document workflows and controls in a way that supports knowledge transfer, audit evidence and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Operations, Payroll, Total Rewards, Equity Administration, Sales Compensation, Tax and Legal so accounting reflects programme changes before they land in the ledger, not after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend workforce accounting processes to new entities and jurisdictions as Anthropic grows internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex compensation accounting into plain language for non-finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop a team of accountants, providing timely, specific feedback that raises the technical and operational bar over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and onboard as the team grows; set clear expectations and build a culture of precision and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move fluidly between reviewing your team&#39;s work and doing the work yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active CPA licence or equivalent professional accounting qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on experience with payroll accounting and stock-based compensation under ASC 718, including equity roll-forwards and reconciliation to an equity administration platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a portfolio of accounts through close in a public company or pre-IPO environment, including designing and operating SOX controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing and maintaining accounting policies and SOPs, and being accountable for how a team applies them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or meaningfully coaching other accountants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous problems, reach defensible conclusions and document them clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication with non-accounting partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial progressive accounting experience that combines Big 4 audit with time at a high-growth or startup company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with commissions accounting (ASC 340-40), contingent worker accounting, or benefits and relocation programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with complex equity structures — preferred stock, tender offers, modifications, or international equity plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing or supporting equity, employee benefit plan and net loss per share disclosures for external reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or contributing to an ERP, payroll, equity or T&amp;amp;E system implementation or integration, particularly where requirements were evolving mid-project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience extending payroll and equity accounting to new entities or countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear point of view on how AI tools can eliminate low-value accounting work, and a track record of putting it into practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is looking for a Senior Partner Account Manager (PAM) to own our relationship with one to two of the world&#39;s largest global systems integrators. This is a general-management role disguised as an alliance role: you will set the multi-year joint strategy with the partner&#39;s C-suite, negotiate the strategic agreement that underpins it, and then build the machine — go-to-market, solution co-development, delivery readiness, and enablement at a scale of tens of thousands of practitioners — that turns Claude into one of the partner&#39;s largest and fastest-growing practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be measured on the size and health of the joint business: progress against a $1B+ Claude practice plan, Anthropic ARR sourced and influenced through the partner, certified and delivery-ready practitioners (50,000+), co-developed solutions in market with reference-able customers, and the depth of executive alignment on both sides.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the joint business.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and run a multi-year joint business plan with each GSI covering services bookings, Anthropic ARR, priority industries and geographies, investment, and headcount. Report on it to Anthropic and partner executive leadership quarterly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead at the C-suite.&lt;/strong&gt; Be the primary Anthropic relationship owner for the partner&#39;s Group CEO, service-line and industry CEOs, CTO/Chief AI Officer, and Chief Learning Officer. Map and activate Anthropic executive sponsors, run CEO-level QBRs, and shape the partner&#39;s public AI narrative (earnings calls, analyst days, flagship events) around Claude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Negotiate the strategic agreement.&lt;/strong&gt; Structure and close multi-year strategic collaboration agreements spanning consumption and resale commitments, co-investment and market development funds, co-marketing, IP and solution terms, and enterprise-wide internal deployment of Claude across the partner&#39;s own workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Co-develop solutions.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Anthropic Product, Applied AI, and the GSI&#39;s CTO office to co-build industry and horizontal offerings, agentic and Claude Code delivery accelerators, and reference architectures; take them to market with named launch customers and published references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build a 50,000+ practitioner practice.&lt;/strong&gt; Design and land a certification and delivery-readiness system inside the partner — embedded in their academy/L&amp;amp;D, train-the-trainer led, tied to Claude Partner Network tier requirements — and hold the partner accountable to capability they build themselves rather than capacity Anthropic supplies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive global co-sell.&lt;/strong&gt; Stand up joint account planning and pursuit governance with Anthropic field leadership across NA, EMEA, and APAC; personally engage on the largest strategic pursuits; ensure clean attribution through deal registration and CRM discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run alliance governance.&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and chair a joint steering committee with named workstreams (GTM, solutions, delivery readiness, enablement, marketing), clear owners on both sides, and a published operating cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead through others.&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate a global virtual team of partner solutions architects, partner marketing, enablement, regional PAMs, and sales leaders; mentor PAMs across the team; scope and make the case for dedicated resourcing as the business scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the program.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring the voice of the largest GSIs into Anthropic&#39;s partner strategy, Elite-tier program design, and product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
