&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and execute a comprehensive marketing strategy for cybersecurity across key segments: enterprise security operations, threat intelligence, detection and response, governance/risk/compliance, MSSPs and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft differentiated positioning and messaging across solutions pages, campaign materials and content for distinct audiences within the vertical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support go-to-market for product and solution launches including sector-specific offerings and relevant MCP integrations and skills (SIEM, SOAR, EDR, threat intelligence platforms, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the alliances team on joint go-to-market with cybersecurity partners, including shared positioning, launch coordination, and integrated campaign moments across security platform and services partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with communications on executive thought leadership regarding AI&#39;s potential to tip the balance toward defenders, including flagship announcements in the context of key security initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the social and content teams on a cybersecurity content calendar that highlights use cases, case studies, and partnership announcements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive thought leadership initiatives and speaking / event opportunities relevant to the security community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable sales teams with compelling materials, outbound campaigns, and pipeline-driving initiatives for security-led enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on which channels and campaigns are driving results and identify opportunities for iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have direct experience marketing software products to security audiences, including familiarity with how CISOs, SOC leaders, and security engineering teams evaluate and buy technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a 0-to-1 environment — can build processes where none exist and navigate ambiguity across a complex stakeholder landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an adaptable generalist with exposure and competency within multiple marketing functions (content, campaigns, social, analytics, sales enablement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong written and verbal communication skills, with an ability to translate complex AI capabilities into clear, compelling narratives for both technical practitioners and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a quick learner who can absorb context on security workflows, buyer dynamics, and compliance frameworks rapidly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excel at cross-functional collaboration — comfortable being the connective tissue between product, sales, partnerships, communications, and marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about AI&#39;s potential to strengthen cyber defense while maintaining focus on responsible, safe deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of marketing experience with at least 2 years of experience in cybersecurity, security operations, or the broader security technology space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked in or with security organizations and understand the distinct priorities and decision-making dynamics of security buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess experience with event marketing at security conferences (e.g., RSA Conference, Black Hat, Gartner Security &amp;amp; Risk, ISAC events)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a background in enterprise sales enablement, particularly in complex or regulated industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show a track record of building marketing programs from scratch at a growth-stage company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate interest in the responsible deployment of AI in security contexts, including an awareness of the dual-use considerations unique to cybersecurity use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
